WEBVTT

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>Half the cherry blossoms around 
Kirishima-Jingu are already in bloom.</i>

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.990
<i>Peak viewing conditions are 
expected by next weekend.</i>

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.860
So tired...

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.110
I figured you'd be here.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.700
What is it, Sae?

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.050
Shiro! We're going to the station now.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.350
Get up, quick!

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.260
I'm too tired to move.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.680
Don't be so lazy!

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.550
Heavy...

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.680
Heavy!

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:42.950
Oh well, I guess we'll just go with Aislinn.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.620
What's at the station?

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.690
We just got a call from Kumakura-sensei.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.300
Toyone is coming today. Officially.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.950
Aww! Shiro, we missed it because of you!

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.530
Do you think Sensei and 
Toyone were on there?

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.270
Probably.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.250
Hey, let's go meet them at the station.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.140
I told them that they didn't 
have to come meet us.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:35.490
Toyone!

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.450
Here I am.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.470
Toyone!

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.080
<i>Now we're five.</i>

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:47.800
<i>Now...</i>

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.830
<i>Everything can begin.</i>

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.010
<b>Saki</b>

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.010
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.180
Venue for the
 West Tokyo 
Regional 
Preliminaries

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.910
<b>Hand 1: 
To Tokyo</b>

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.230
Riichi!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.730
A double-riichi!

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.960
Shiraitodai's fifth player, Oohoshi Awai,

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.730
already sailed through the first 
half of the match on top.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.240
She's taking out some insurance 
with this double-riichi!

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:24.660
Kan!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:31.750
Tsumo!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.250
3,000. 6,000.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.010
And it's over!

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.510
For the third year in a row, 
Shiraitodai High School

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.640
is the West Tokyo representative at nationals!

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.640
Shiraitodai High School 
1st Year
 Oohoshi Awai

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.100
Shiraitodai High School 
2nd Year
 Matano Seiko

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.460
While Shiraitodai's second team is also considered 
prefectural representative strength,

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.520
Shiraitodai High School 
2nd Year
 Shibuya Takami

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.520
this "Team Torahime" is in

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.940
an entirely different league!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.940
Shiraitodai High School 
3rd Year
 Hirose Sumire

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.020
The one leading the team stands

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.650
at the pinnacle of all 10,000 high schoolers!

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.350
If you talk about the 
inter-high school tournament,

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.780
you're talking about her.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.900
The current champion, Miyanaga Teru!

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.480
They've made their move toward 
a new record of winning

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.950
Shiraitodai High School 
3rd Year
 Miyanaga Teru

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.870
the nationals three times in a row!

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.200
There it is!

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.200
Arena for the
 East Tokyo
 Regional 
Preliminaries

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.290
We just witnessed the birth of 
the strongest team in East Tokyo!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.790
Analyst / Professional Mahjong player
 Kokaji Sukoya

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.790
Commentary / Announcer
 Fukuyo Kouko

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.240
Rinkai Girls' has represented 
their region 15 years in a row!

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.920
That's our pro player Kokaji! 
She's got her facts straight!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.330
That means this is their 16th 
year representing East Tokyo!

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.650
Are you really an announcer?

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.250
But you know, they do have a lot
of foreigners on their team.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.440
<b>Rinkai Girls'</b>

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.440
You're right.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.420
But starting this year,

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.740
there's a rule that you can't 
have an exchange student

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.590
be the first player.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.950
Until last year, Rinkai only had 
exchange students on their team.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.850
You're right, that's unfair and 
downright mean, huh?

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.000
I didn't say that!

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.850
But this team is really strong.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.310
The only Japanese player 
on their team, Tsujigaito,

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.180
came in third in last year's 
individual tournament.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.790
Rinkai Girls' 3rd Year
 Tsujigaito Satoha

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.900
Davin, from the USA,
 will be playing in

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.340
Rinkai Girls' 3rd Year

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.340
the team matches, 
like last year.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.890
But it's the three new scholarship students 
who are drawing the world's attention.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:09.850
Hao, from Hong Kong, won the silver 
medal at the Asian tournament in Inchon.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.850
Rinkai Girls' 1st Year
 Hao Huiyu

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.270
From Sakartvelo, 
we have Virsaladz,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.600
Rinkai Girls' 1st Year

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.600
who made a name for herself at 
the World Junior Tournament.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.630
Choe Myenonghwa from France 
earned herself the title

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.310
of "Venter," or "The God of Wind," 
at the European championship,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.110
Rinkai Girls' 2nd Year
 Choe Myenonghwa

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.570
and places high in the worldwide ranking.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.720
Worldwide ranking?! Wow, really?! 
How about you?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.370
Me?

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.690
Well, I haven't played in many tournaments

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.730
that would be pertinent to that ranking...

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.380
When I last looked at the site, I was ranked 973.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.340
And this concludes our broadcast!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.900
Kagoshima

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.260
A direct yakuman hit ends it!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.560
The prefectural preliminaries are over

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.320
without ever reaching the fifth player!

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.560
Just like last year, Kagoshima will 
be represented by Eisui Girls'!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.560
Eisui Girls' 3rd Year
 Usuzumi Hatsumi

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:02.400
I hear that Usuzumi often wins 
when she is in the North seat.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.980
What is your take on this, 
pro player Oonuma?

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.820
<i>The North seat exposes her tiles between</i>

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.830
<i>the East seat and the North seat...</i>

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.580
<i>The North-East Gate of Evil...</i>

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.660
The rest of her tiles are then the reverse,
the South-West Gate of Evil...

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.340
I don't quite get what you mean,

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.720
but Usuzumi's South-West 
Gate of Evil decided it this time!

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.220
Eisui Girls' will be going 
to the Nationals once more!

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.640
I'm back.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.540
Good work.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.450
Good work, Hacchan.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.360
Is the princess resting?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.020
Eisui Girls' 3rd Year
 Karijuku Tomoe

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.020
Yes, she had to.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:47.710
I don't know if I should be happy 
or sad that I didn't have to play.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:48.530
Eisui Girls' 1st Year
 Takimi Haru

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:48.530
Eisui Girls' 3rd Year
 Iwato Kasumi

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.120
It's good when it's over quickly, isn't it?

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.620
I mean...

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:59.550
All of us from different branch families are here 
together this year. And do you know why?

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.140
So our Princess doesn't have 
to overdo it like last year.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:05.030
Eisui Girls' 2nd Year
 Jindai Komaki

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.760
Let's just keep going like this and 
win the Nationals without hassle.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.260
Ron.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:12.790
2,000.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.930
Himematsu High School (South Osaka)
 3rd Year
 Suehara Kyouko

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:15.930
That's it!

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.730
All right!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.730
Himematsu High School (South Osaka) 
3rd Year
 Atago Hiroe

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.990
Himematsu High School's fifth player, 
Suehara, carefully ends it with a hidden tenpai.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.270
Himematsu High School (South Osaka)
 2nd Year
 Atago Kinue

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.450
I knew Suehara-senpai would do it.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.150
Himematsu High School (South Osaka)
2nd Year
 Ueshige Suzu

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.150
Himematsu High School (South Osaka) 
3rd Year
 Mase Yuuko

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.150
In the end, though, their lead is huge!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:31.020
This year's rep for South Osaka 
is Himematsu High School, again!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.850
August
Nagano

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:58.960
Good morning.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.890
Good morning.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.400
It's finally time.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.190
Yes.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.750
<i>Finally the Nationals.</i>

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.070
<i>I can see my sister!</i>

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:24.800
Healthy and ample,

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.840
it's Inter-high Tournament Radio!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.810
Here again this week, the 
not-so-ample super announcer,

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.460
Fukuyo Kouko, and...

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:37.030
The not-so-healthy Kokaji Sukoya.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.430
We'll be keeping you updated 
on the inter-high tournament.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.250
By the way, you received a silver 
medal in Rio de Janeiro's

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.870
East Match Freestyle, as well as 
other glamorous achievements.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.360
Where's this coming from?

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.850
Lately, you've been playing 
for a local club team

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:54.490
and are quite far away from any title, right?

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.670
All that set-up just to criticize me?!

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.010
But apparently,

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.370
the reason for that was to save 
a local club from likely ruin.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.210
I've heard you're very popular with the locals,

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.690
especially the children.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.290
And let's not forget that you
won the inter-high tournament

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.830
20 years ago!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.110
I just read about it on the web!

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.010
It was only 10 years ago!

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.930
I don't even like to say that...

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:23.940
Once again this year,

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:29.400
students from 3,000 schools have 
fought hard all across the nation,

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:35.450
and the representative schools who won 
those tough regional tournaments

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.200
are arriving here in Tokyo, one after another!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.970
We're finally here, Tokyo!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.530
Well, it's Shinjuku.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:49.240
Hmm... Our transfer is this way.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:15.890
We finally made it.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:16.800
It's big!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.780
Where's Kyoutarou?

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.220
Suga-kun's in a single room 
in the other building.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.510
Now,

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.480
until tomorrow's opening ceremony, 
you're free to do what you like.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.090
Of course, don't go overboard 
and end up exhausted tomorrow.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.160
Yay!

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.390
Nodo-chan, Saki-chan!
 Come with me!

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.020
Zoom!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.800
Where are you going, Yuuki?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.710
Isn't that obvious?!

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:44.330
Are you sure about this?

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.380
Yes.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:48.120
We have to get used to living here first.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.960
It's a long way to the finals.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.390
You're right.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.430
<b>Bath</b>

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.140
Bath!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.760
There are other people, 
so be a little quieter.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:10.980
Yuuki-chan sure loves the bath.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.120
Yup.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.130
Not as much as tacos, though.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:18.310
You're just as loud as always, 
tacos girl from Kiyosumi.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.880
You ruined my heavenly bathtime.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:24.320
Who are you?!

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.380
Have you been well?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:31.680
Oh, you're Kazekoshi's... Ikeda or something.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.350
We fought over food at the 
mixed training camp, remember?

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:38.420
And be more polite to your upperclassmen.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.610
Ikeda, what are you doing here?

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:43.640
I'm here with Captain, who will be 
playing in the individual tournament.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:44.430
Huh?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.930
Then does that mean...

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.180
Yes.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.090
The rooms for Kazekoshi and 
Kiyosumi are next to each other.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.800
Koromo's here, too!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.030
We're here.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.160
Hello.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.340
What? Ryuumonbuchi is here, too?

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.030
Yes.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:26.010
They're staying in a hotel in Shinjuku.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.880
Damn rich folks...

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.480
Apparently, the people from Tsuruga

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.640
will also come once they know 
when our first match is.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.090
Really?

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:37.480
So it'll be just like the mixed training camp.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:39.910
Kind of anticlimactic...

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.400
Takes away the excitement a little.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.280
Saki!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.030
K-Koromo-chan...

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.910
But I'm kind of jealous.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.120
When I was a first year, 
our senpais were really strict.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.440
The farewell party, coming to Tokyo,

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.130
the lottery and opening ceremony...

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.390
On the day of the first 
match, the first years

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:02.710
were already destroyed 
by all the pressure.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:06.720
I guess staying focused at 
all times might be rough.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.350
The earliest matches will 
be the day after tomorrow.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:14.020
That might be especially true if 
you intend to go to the finals.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:24.250
<i>This might work to loosen up the 
first years, but what about you?</i>

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.840
Let's all do our best.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.400
Let's.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.870
Umm...

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.370
Speaking of, where's Coach?

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.730
In the advisor room in building D.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.630
Let's go say hi later.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:47.090
I see. Sorry for piling that on you.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.540
Oh, no, it's fine.

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:52.370
But only this year, all right?

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:52.890
Huh?

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.890
Next year, we're all going.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.670
Damn you, Bundou. 
You really do get it, don't you?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.940
Oh, Saki-chan, good morning.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.290
It's morning?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.590
Are we in Tokyo?

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.460
Yup!

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.130
The lottery is at nine.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.760
Get ready quickly.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:30.520
Yes! You're right!

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.860
I can see the moat and the stone wall!

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.630
Is that a castle?

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:52.480
Yes...

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.410
It used to be.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.620
Now that's a park.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.250
Really?

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.360
If we can get in, 
let's go there later!

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.310
If we have time.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:05.530
Really?

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.550
Now I really feel like we're in Tokyo.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:11.980
Yeah.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:15.450
Yesterday we went straight to our hotel.

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:23.550
We're here!

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.650
It's big!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.420
We will begin the lottery shortly.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.820
It really is different from Nagano.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:35.530
Would the representatives for each school 
please gather in the indicated waiting room?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.510
Where is Saki-chan?

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:37.330
Don't tell me...

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.460
She's lost again?!

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.210
Where am I?

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.630
I got lost again...

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.910
Maybe it's this way.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.960
What are we going to do if 
we happen to run into Nodoka?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.070
Then we can't help it.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.800
It might really happen.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.870
We do want to see her 
sooner rather than later.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.460
<i>Did I imagine that?</i>

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:52.820
South Osaka, Himematsu High School, #38.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.750
That's quite a reaction.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:57.970
Obviously.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.580
It's totally out of place 
for them to not be a seed.

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:06.640
Since Eisui came on the scene last 
year, they stopped being a seed,

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.990
but if anything, they're 
a powerhouse that's easily

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:10.870
in the top five of the 52 
best schools in the country.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.490
Based on the preliminary 
lottery, the next should be...

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:17.720
Nagano, Kiyosumi High.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.930
Our pres is totally nervous!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.470
That's unusual.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.340
#33.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.390
<i>Not a single peep.</i>

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:29.800
<i>Quite a difference from Himematsu.</i>

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.790
<i>I guess that's to be expected.</i>

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.240
Wait, #33?

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.880
That means...

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.090
<i>Ouch.</i>

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:44.780
<i>We're in the same block as the team 
that got the big reaction, Himematsu,</i>

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:46.120
<i>and the 3rd seed...</i>

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:50.000
<i>Eisui Girls'!</i>

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:51.270
All right!

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:54.200
Here at the the National 
High School Mahjong Tournament,

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:57.260
the final number has been drawn...

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:02.310
and the final spots in the tournament 
brackets have been filled!

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:07.020
Behold, this is the ladder of destiny!

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.500
Which high school will stand 
at the top of this ladder?!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.720
This will be a hot summer 
for the 48 schools!

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.640
Hey, Kouko-chan...

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:18.030
What, should I have said 
bracket instead of ladder?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.660
No, that doesn't matter.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.830
But it's 52 schools, not 48.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:28.140
But the lottery and the first round 
matches have just 48 schools.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:32.190
That's because the four seeded 
schools are not taking part...

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.550
but I already explained this on the radio!

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.300
Why are those four schools so special?

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:43.400
They're chosen from the 52 schools 
who won their regional tournaments,

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:45.630
based on the results of last 
year's inter-high tournament

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.570
and the spring tournament.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.980
<i>Being a seed doesn't mean you're 
exempt from the preliminaries.</i>

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:52.820
Wahaha, I see.

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:54.710
That's how it works.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:57.630
It almost feels like she's tricking 
her into explaining this.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.600
Kouko-chan isn't that clever.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.590
But now we know when 
Kiyosumi will be playing.

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.500
The first match will be on the third day.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:10.500
If they make it to the finals, 
it'll be seven days.

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:15.210
Normally that would mean the cost 
of lodging would be ridiculous.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.970
Kanbara, are you sure it's okay?

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.830
Wahaha, sort of.

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:24.200
My grandma in Monnaka 
pestered me to come early.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.930
The building is old, but it's 
got an AC and lots of room.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.370
Wahaha, so we just have 
to worry about food.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.590
We'll be relying on Kanbara a lot.

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:39.030
We will now commence 
the opening ceremony of the

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.970
National High School 
Mahjong Tournament.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.410
It is finally time to raise the curtain

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.130
for this summer's National 
High School Mahjong Tournament!

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.000
Which school will be the one to seize

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.130
the top spot in this year's tournament?

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:58.970
A hot summer for the students 
aiming to be best in the nation

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.300
is beginning now!

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:14.690
Good work at the lottery 
and the opening ceremony.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.800
Especially Nodoka, for the interviews,

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.070
and Saki, for being lost.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.440
You, too.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.640
I'm glad we found you before 
the opening ceremony.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:27.020
Our first match is on the third day,

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:29.200
so we don't have any matches 
tomorrow and the day after that.

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:32.040
In order to avoid losing our edge before then,

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.310
there will be a minimal regimen.

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.210
However, tomorrow morning 
will be for resting.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:41.940
You're free to view the opening 
matches, or go check out the city.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:44.150
You can also stay here and sleep.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:48.210
Eating tacos at a Mexican 
restaurant's okay, too!

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:49.680
Oh, right!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.430
I have to return this skirt 
to you, Someya-senpai.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.020
What's going on?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.480
When I was still half-asleep, 
I accidentally put it on.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:01.340
It looks good on you.
 Why don't you keep it on?

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:02.490
It looks good.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.490
I agree.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.820
You think so?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.090
I told you to keep it on!

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:11.890
Saki-san!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.830
Saki-chan, we can see everything!

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:17.270
<i>I wonder if this will be the last 
time we can all relax and have fun.</i>

00:22:56.420 --> 00:23:00.060
All right, we're heading out. 
Got everything?

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:03.870
I'm tired. Carry me.

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:05.440
Get up already!

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:08.410
I wonder what kind of 
people we'll play today.

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:10.620
I'm super excited!

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.080
Super excited!

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:18.590
Yes.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.330
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Kosegawa Shiromi

00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:24.090
It doesn't matter who we play.

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:24.090
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Kakura Kurumi

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:25.840
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:27.590
Enjoying ourselves and 
winning is what we,

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.590
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Anetai Toyone

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:31.250
Miyamori Girls', do!

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:34.970
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Usuzawa Sae

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Support</b>

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:39.810
Nodoka-chan, the mixed training camp 
with the four schools was fun, huh?

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:42.810
Yes, we were able to get a lot of
valuable experience before the Nationals.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:43.850
The Nationals...

00:23:43.850 --> 00:23:45.580
I will defeat...

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:47.800
everything... to fight my sister.

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:49.110
Saki-san?

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:55.250
<b>Watch again!</b>
